SUMMARY: Frequency: Latavia
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Frequency — a monthly live music series at Worth 
 Gallery. Frequency spotlights BIPOC musicians of varying genres through i
 ntimate\, stripped-back shows. Celebrating sound\, connection\, and creat
 ive expression in Toronto's vibrant music scene. Find your new favorite m
 usician in your new favorite gallery.\n\n\nThis edition of Frequency feat
 ures Latavia\, a powerhouse vocalist who offers healing through lyrics an
 d melody.\n\n\nLatavia is an R&B/Soul singer-songwriter from Brampton\, O
 ntario. Growing up in her grandfather's church\, she began singing at the
  age of four and writing lyrics at age nine. Drawing inspiration from '90
 s and early 2000's R&B\, she is influenced by iconic vocalists such as Wh
 itney Houston\, Brandy and Jazmine Sullivan\, artists known for their emo
 tional vulnerability\, powerful vocals and raw storytelling. She creates 
 emotionally honest music about self-worth\, love\, heartbreak\, and perso
 nal growth. Through her artistry\, Latavia aims to inspire healing\, refl
 ection and empowerment. She has new music set to be released this year.\n
 \n\nLocated in the lower gallery — down a flight of stairs.\nFor any othe
 r accessibility questions\, please feel free to reach out to us.
CATEGORIES:Concert,Art-Show/Gallery-Event,Worth-Gallery
